  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0126_b8f447b3385c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 288px;\" /><br />Recall the formula of the magnitude of the magnetic field in terms of current and permeability in free space,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;"
  }
